# plans/VALUES_BY_DEFAULT.md §6 "Decision 46": YO_AUDIT_RC_WRITE lists every
# write through a reference cell that reaches codegen, without failing. With
# the `ref(struct(...))` form deleted (v0.2.79) no user-spelled write
# through a counted handle reaches codegen — an `Rc`/`Arc` payload is
# read-only through the handle (E0919), a `RefCell` door's write is behind
# the door, and `Rc.make_mut`'s result is a value place — so the census is
# EMPTY for user code and this fixture pins the negatives. The golden is the
# whole (empty) output: the C goes to a file (no `--emit-c`), and the
# rejected write inside `comptime_expect_error` is not listed
# (issues/fixed/2026-11-19-the-rc-write-census-lists-a-write-inside-comptime-expect-error.md).
env=YO_AUDIT_RC_WRITE=1
timeout=120
